   "text": {
    "L1": "India is home to hundreds of languages and dialects. The Constitution lists 22 languages.",
    "L2": "Hindi is spoken by the largest number of people, but most Indians have a different mother tongue.",
    "L3": "So the belief that Hindi is everyone’s home language is not true. Many people speak two or three languages.",
    "L4": "Different regions also have their own dances, music and foods. This variety is part of India’s richness.",
    "L5": "For example, Assam has Bihu and pitha, Gujarat has Garba and dhokla, and Tamil Nadu has Bharatanatyam and idli.",
    "L6": "People can share words, food, music and festivals across regions. Every language and culture deserves equal respect.",
    "L7": "Notice the pattern: differences make India varied, and sharing makes it richer."
   },
